  "reason": "Evidence: The best configuration so far is config_049 (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted) at 0.725 acc. We've established that transformer aggregation + weighted fusion + imagenet_vit_l is the strongest architecture, and scvi_n200 >> scgpt as RNA encoder. The one untested RNA encoder in this proven architecture is pca_n2000. This experiment tests whether pca_n2000 can match or exceed scvi_n200 within the best-known architecture (transformer + weighted + imagenet_vit_l). It is the best use of this slot because it stays in the high-performing region (low risk of a large drop), reduces uncertainty about the RNA encoder choice, and if pca_n2000 performs comparably it opens flexibility for the remaining 3 experiments, while if it underperforms it firmly confirms scvi_n200 as the optimal encoder so remaining budget can focus on other refinements."
}

